  "can_do": [
    "I can give instructions and rules with the imperative (<i>Open, Don't run</i>).",
    "I can suggest doing something together with <i>Let's</i> and <i>Let's not</i>.",
    "I can understand instructions on signs, in recipes and in games."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "An imperative has no subject — start straight with the verb: <i>Open, Close, Listen</i>.",
    "Negative imperative: <b>Don't</b> + base verb.",
    "<i>Let's</i> (let us) + base verb is a suggestion for you and everyone together.",
    "Negative suggestion: <b>Let's not</b> — never <i>Let's don't</i>.",
    "<i>Please</i> makes an instruction more polite; it can go at the start or the end."
  ]
}
